# A typed table's row policy judges a read on the stored row, an add on the
# new row, a delete on the stored row, and a put over a row on the stored row
# and then the new one; a put under a new key is an insert. The first owner of
# a project is let in by a policy that reads the project row written earlier
# in the same transaction and finds no member yet, since the row it judges is
# not written. A row the caller may not read is never returned, and a refused
# write is `Denied`. The same lines print at O0, O1 and O2.
fixture: RowPolicyJudgesEachOperation.fixture
env: NO_COLOR=1
step default: jet run main.jet
exit: 0
stdout: = row_policy_judges_each_operation.stdout.expected
step: jet build main.jet
exit: 0
step debug: built
exit: 0
stdout: == default
step release: jet run --release main.jet
exit: 0
stdout: == default
